WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.920
There's a language barrier inside the walls
of our schools and it's not going away.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.000
In fact, the volume of students who arrive
in classrooms

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.051
without the native language in their toolkit
is steadily increasing.

00:00:17.051 --> 00:00:21.050
In the United States, the number of English
Language Learners

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:26.640
and the nation's k-12 student population has
more than doubled since 1990.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.540
When students aren't able to comprehend a
new language,

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.940
it can be difficult to socialize with peers,
or understand new concepts.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.660
Often these students feel disconnected from
their school community.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.920
Sometimes, despite a teacher's best efforts
to explain something,

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.780
students with a language barriers still feel
lost.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:51.039
With Microsoft Translator, teachers can easily
engage students regardless of their language

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:52.239
abilities.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:57.239
Teachers simply "tap" to start a conversation,
and share the code with their students.

00:00:57.239 --> 00:00:59.359
Students join the conversation by entering
the code

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:02.720
into any device with web capability.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.680
Then they choose which language they would
like to hear or see.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.160
As the teacher speaks, Translator provides
real-time audio

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.330
in the chosen language for each student.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:17.220
It also provides a live, real-time transcript
of the conversation.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.690
Students can hear and read the conversation
as it is happening in class.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.400
The transcript appears on a student's device
in the language of their choice.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:31.240
In fact, Microsoft Translator can translate
into multiple languages simultaneously.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.750
This live translation allows students to be
fully engaged

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:40.100
in the topics and social dynamics of the classroom.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.880
Translation can be tricky with unique names
or subject specific vocabulary.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.750
But with the PowerPoint add-in, Translator
reads everything in the teacher's side deck

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:54.140
and slide nodes so it can create a more accurate
translation.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.610
Translator gives me the opportunity to reach
my students

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.080
in a way I never could before.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.500
I love seeing their faces light up when they
realized they

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.860
actually understand the message I'm trying
to get across.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:09.170
They can participate in class discussions
like never before.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:12.810
Translation doesn't only accommodate the learning
of non-native speakers.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.110
It helps other students, too.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:19.860
Taking notes in class can be a challenge,
but the transcripts provided by Microsoft

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.540
Translator
allow all students to access the conversation

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.940
after the fact.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.540
Microsoft Translator allows students to move
from feeling confused

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:33.140
to feeling connected with peers and engaged
in learning.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.110
Translator saves time, provides real-time
translation,

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:41.010
and keeps students captivated with classroom
conversations.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:47.500
Just visit aka.ms/translatoredu to learn more
and download the app.

